This game is frankly a good idea hampered by the simple fact of money, or lack of it. The game is written like a cheesier version of Uncharted and the plot ends up going slightly mad towards the rather abrupt ending caused by what I guess would be a sudden lack of money forcing Air Tight to piece together what they had in the hopes they could salvage something.
However the one thing this game has going for it is the jetpack gameplay which is honestly seamless and fantasticly fun to grind Will's face on a wall because you accidently activated the jetpack indoors. I would recomend this game but honestly don't expect a long fantastic game it's a good little bit of fun if you treat it like that and keep in mind they ran out of money so go easy on Dark Void, it is trying as best it can.
