I've been playing guitar since 2003 (bass since 2012) and I truely enjoy playing this game. This is by far the most enjoyable way to learn new songs, and the variety of genres (dlc included) is pretty awesome.
The game starts off at a reasonable challenge level and ramps you up. During that time I've noticed with some songs it makes you play more complicated 'weird' riffs before you get to the actual way the riff is played, which is about my only complaint.
With the bass expansion jamming with friends is really fun, but if you have a really lose set of bass strings tunning--especially low tunnings can be a pain to get where the game will let you progress.
@_@;;
